 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$ f=12\\ln u,\\,u=2 x.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{12}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{u}\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{2 x}\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{x}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=12$ is\n\n$$m=\\left.(\\frac{12}{x})\\right|_{x=12}=1.$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(12,12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)})$ is $m=1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}) &=(1)(x-(12)) \\\\ y &=x - 12 + 12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}$$" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490401 1080 "y=x + 12" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490401 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490401 1083 #uuid "275a4506-33ca-5ecb-9e05-16f411b46fa5" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490402 1080 "y=2 x - 6 - \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490402 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490402 1083 #uuid "3555aad0-2803-578b-8e25-d9b747f8b523" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490403 1080 "y=x - 12" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490403 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490403 1083 #uuid "3dd44058-54a0-5bdc-983f-368f2dce91f1" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490404 1080 "y=20 - x" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490404 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490404 1083 #uuid "40aabc0b-b390-5fc8-8a17-fa253d00fd29" 13194139535281 17592186045443 true] [17592186490405 1080 "y=x + 2